## USAGE INSTRUCTIONS

### For LaTeX Documents:

1. Save this file as `references.bib` in your LaTeX project directory

2. In your main .tex file, add:
```latex
\bibliographystyle{ieeetr}  % or apalike, plain, etc.
\bibliography{references}
```

3. Cite papers using:
```latex
\cite{goodfellow2015explaining}
\cite{madry2018towards}
\cite{he2016deep,krizhevsky2009learning,nicolae2019adversarial}
```

4. Compile with:
```bash
pdflatex main.tex
bibtex main
pdflatex main.tex
pdflatex main.tex
```

### For Overleaf:

1. Upload this file to your Overleaf project
2. Use the same citation commands as above
3. Overleaf will automatically compile the bibliography

### For Citation Managers (Zotero, Mendeley, EndNote):

1. Import this .bib file directly
2. The citation manager will parse all entries
3. Use for citations in Word/Google Docs with plugins

